    "chromium": {
      "$comment": "OPTIONAL: the Playwright chromium build (decision 13). Replaces the installers' `npx playwright install chromium` ladders: those fetch whatever revision the npm-resolved playwright wants, unverified, and hang on apt releases playwright does not recognize (#35166). The pin version IS playwright's chromium revision, and it must equal the revision in the root package-lock's playwright-core browsers.json (chromium 1208 = browserVersion 145.0.7632.6, playwright 1.58.2) -- enforced by tests/test_chromium_pin_lockstep.py: bump playwright and this pin in ONE commit or CI fails. x64/mac/win are Chrome-for-Testing zips on the bare cdn keyed by browserVersion; linux-arm64 is the classic revision path (playwright-core's own DOWNLOAD_PATHS split). No win32-arm64 build exists upstream -- that target keeps the system-browser rung. STORE LAYOUT EXCEPTION: playwright resolves browsers by directory name under PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH, so these entries are named playwright's way in the shared store (chromium-1208/, no target suffix -- store_entry_name special-cases it) and installation/env.py points PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH at the store root. No links (banned), no per-install copies. Archives keep their internal layout (chrome-linux64/chrome etc.), and the entry gets playwright's INSTALLATION_COMPLETE marker so its registry trusts the dir. Known hazard, accepted: a hand-run `npx playwright install` from a DIFFERENT playwright version may GC entries whose revision it does not expect; the facts detect the vanish and the next sweep reprovisions. onPath false: a browser tree is not a CLI surface.",
      "version": "1208",
      "optional": true,
      "onPath": false,
